      "body": "<!-- open-swe-review-comment {\"id\":\"f_3f966a0883\",\"file_path\":\"libs/sdk-py/langgraph_sdk/encryption/types.py\",\"start_line\":80,\"end_line\":82,\"side\":\"RIGHT\"} -->\n\n🟡 **Decorator widens existing handler return types**\n\nChanging `BlobDecryptor` to return the union also widens every function passed through `@encryption.decrypt.blob`, because that decorator is declared to return `types.BlobDecryptor` rather than the input callable's precise type. Consequently, existing code such as `value: bytes = await decrypt(...)` now fails static checking even when `decrypt` is explicitly annotated `-> bytes` (the checker reports `bytes | DecryptResult[bytes]`); the same regression occurs for `JsonDecryptor` at lines 127-129. Preserve the decorated callable's concrete return type (for example with a callable type variable/overloads) while storing it internally under the broader handler type, so raw-return handlers remain source-compatible as intended.\n\n*(Refers to lines 80-82)*\n\n---\n*Your feedback helps Open SWE learn. React with 👍 or 👎 to tell us if this review comment was useful.*",
